WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.963
You get one glance at a headline.

00:00:02.103 --> 00:00:03.980
Who do you think did something wrong?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.400
Hold that thought.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.152
We matched thirty-two weeks of archived
homepages.

00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:15.095
Migration appeared on fifteen BBC dates,
eleven ITV dates and five Channel Four
dates.

00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:18.520
Scrutiny of Reform conduct appeared on one,
two and five.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.628
Then we looked closer.

00:00:20.768 --> 00:00:26.315
Between October the sixteenth and November
the eighteenth, we matched a hundred and
eleven desktop checks.

00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:28.631
Twenty-one scheduled checks had gaps.

00:00:28.771 --> 00:00:30.691
Here’s what the first screen showed.

00:00:31.391 --> 00:00:34.911
On the BBC, applicants appeared to be
posing as experts.

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:39.573
Four hours later, the same investigation
led with a firm offering fake art.

00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:40.887
Same story.

00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:42.861
Who sounds responsible now?

00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:47.636
The BBC had one check explicitly portraying
migrants negatively.

00:00:47.776 --> 00:00:49.589
A broader reading gives five.

00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:53.015
For alleged Reform wrongdoing, the counts
were zero and one.

00:00:53.715 --> 00:00:57.427
On ITV, a Reform hopeful called for
migrants to be confined.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.572
Three checks carried that rhetoric.

00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:01.867
Whose conduct was the story questioning?

00:01:02.007 --> 00:01:03.095
The speaker’s.

00:01:03.235 --> 00:01:08.312
ITV had five checks scrutinising Reform and
none directly blaming migrants.

00:01:09.012 --> 00:01:15.049
Channel Four kept one undercover
investigation into foreign donations on the
first screen at every check.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:17.749
A hundred and eleven appearances of one
story.

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:21.516
The headline raised suspicion without
naming a specific breach.

00:01:22.216 --> 00:01:25.032
Next time you open the news, pick the first
headline.

00:01:25.172 --> 00:01:26.367
Find the verb.

00:01:26.507 --> 00:01:27.829
Who gets the blame?

00:01:27.969 --> 00:01:30.487
Would you judge another outlet by the same
rule?

00:01:30.627 --> 00:01:32.845
Play the challenge at Coding for Justice.
